</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_flow_through_choke" target="ai_economic_shift::infra_invest_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A persistent reduction in oil flow through the choke forces longer shipping routes, raises logistics and construction input costs and causes permitting/insurance delays, which raises capex per project and slows the pace of new AI data‑center and related infrastructure builds.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_flow_through_choke" target="shipping_chokepoints::global_freight_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher uninterrupted oil throughput preserves tanker availability and bunker supply stability, reducing displacement of tonnage onto longer routes and lowering shipping cost pressures that push up freight rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::oil_flow_through_choke" target="us_china_tech_trade::private_fin_mobil" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained reduction in oil throughput raises energy price volatility and supply uncertainty for manufacturers and logistics providers, reducing projected returns and increasing perceived project risk, which causes private investors to delay or scale back mobilization for large cross‑border tech and supply‑chain investments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
