<edge source="us_iran_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in maritime incidents disrupts hardware shipments (GPUs, accelerators) and increases delivery uncertainty, causing firms to shift from on‑prem purchases to renting cloud compute, thereby raising demand intensity for cloud/hosted AI compute.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_export_throughp" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising rate of hostile incidents in a major chokepoint forces shipowners/insurers to reroute, delay or avoid calling at higher-risk regional ports and reallocates available tonnage, reducing effective export throughput from other contested maritime corridors including the Black Sea.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="shipping_chokepoints::global_freight_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in hostile or disruptive incidents raises insurance and security premiums, forces longer detours and slower operations, and thus raises per-voyage and spot freight prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" target="us_china_tech_trade::component_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in hostile or disruptive maritime incidents causes voyage cancellations, port closures, carrier blank sailings and higher insurance refusals that directly delay or cancel shipments of critical components along the Asia–US trade lanes, reducing on‑hand and pipeline component availability.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
