</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="ai_economic_shift::capital_inflow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A more effective blockade raises regional conflict and shipping-insurance risk premiums, prompting global and regional investors to pull back or delay equity and debt financing into AI firms and projects with supply‑chain or regional exposure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_missile_strike_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A materially more effective blockade in the Gulf draws U.S./NATO naval and air assets (surveillance, escorts, strike-capable ships) into the Persian Gulf, reducing allied deterrence and ISR in the Black Sea and thereby enabling Russia to increase the tempo of drone and missile strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="shipping_chokepoints::chokepoint_congestion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater blockade effectiveness directly reduces permitted transits and forces vessels to wait or queue at chokepoint approaches, producing immediate backlogs and flow restriction.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="shipping_chokepoints::supply_chain_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">More effective interdiction undermines predictability and throughput of scheduled shipments (imports/exports and input flows), eroding firms' ability to absorb disruptions and recover from shocks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" target="us_china_tech_trade::tariff_enforce_int" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater interdiction effectiveness exposes routes and firms attempting to circumvent sanctions or controls, prompting customs and trade authorities to tighten inspections and apply tariffs and border measures more rigorously to prevent embargo/Sanctions leakage.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::shipping_insurance_premi" target="concept::shipping_insurance_premium_l" id="0">
  <data key="d28">instance_of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" target="us_iran_standoff::domestic_political_press" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" target="us_iran_standoff::market_contagion_intensi" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" target="ai_economic_shift::asset_valuations_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher global oil prices feed into inflation and higher real discount rates and operating cost expectations, compressing valuation multiples on growth assets including publicly and privately held AI companies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher global oil (and related hydrocarbon) prices improve Russia's fiscal position and room for maneuver, increasing its capacity and incentive to modulate or curtail deliveries as a political/economic lever, thereby increasing disruptions and variability in regional energy flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" target="us_china_tech_trade::supply_reconfig_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in benchmark oil prices raises shipping and operating costs, creating stronger near‑term economic incentives for firms to accelerate sourcing and logistics redesign (nearshoring, alternative routes, inventory strategy changes) to limit fuel exposure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
