<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Disruptions and price spikes in regional energy flows force rationing, higher operating costs and increased outage risk for data centers, reducing the volume/length of large-scale training runs and overall intensity of compute demand in affected zones.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="shipping_chokepoints::global_freight_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Disruptions to regional energy exports force longer tanker routings, raise bunker fuel price volatility and insurance premiums, and thereby push up average global freight rates for affected lanes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="us_china_tech_trade::private_fin_mobil" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Recurrent disruptions to energy exports increase volatility and reveal supply‑security gaps, prompting private investors to commit capital into strategic energy and resilience projects (LNG, storage, domestic capacity and related industrial onshoring) that reallocate private financing relevant to US–China tech/industrial competition.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="us_china_tech_trade::tariff_enforce_int" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute interruptions in energy commodity flows lead governments to impose or more rigorously apply border measures and export restrictions to protect domestic supply, thereby increasing tariff and related enforcement intensity on affected product flows between major trading partners.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Cuts or volatility in Russian energy exports directly tighten global supply expectations, causing benchmark crude prices to rise.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_flow_disruption" target="us_iran_standoff::oil_flow_through_choke" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Disruptions to Russian export routes force refiners and traders to reroute crude and products via alternative passages, increasing volumes transiting the strategic choke point in the US–Iran theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
