<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::supply_reconfig_rate" target="shipping_chokepoints::chokepoint_congestion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid corporate rerouting and relocation of sourcing concentrates previously dispersed container and breakbulk flows through alternative straits and ports, producing immediate backlogs and queuing at those chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::supply_reconfig_rate" target="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Faster firm-level reconfiguration of supply chains away from standard, heavily policed routes increases use of smaller ships, alternative ports and opaque transshipment nodes that are harder for interdiction forces to monitor, reducing the practical effectiveness of any blockade or interdiction campaign.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
