<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::geo_risk_percep" target="ai_economic_shift::asset_valuations_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in perceived geopolitical risk raises investor risk premia for firms with cross‑border exposure (supply, markets, IP), causing multiples and market valuations for AI‑related assets to compress as buyers reprice uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::geo_risk_percep" target="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_export_throughp" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in geopolitical risk perception tied to US–China tech/trade tensions raises insurer premiums and routing risk assessments, prompting shipping companies and freight forwarders to reroute or suspend calls through nearby regional maritime corridors (including Black Sea access points), reducing throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::geo_risk_percep" target="shipping_chokepoints::foreign_investment_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising geopolitical risk perception leads investors and funds to delay, scale back or withdraw cross-border commitments, producing an observable drop in inbound foreign investment and increased capital flight.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::geo_risk_percep" target="us_iran_standoff::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in perceived geopolitical risk from US–China tech/trade friction will prompt traders and oil market participants to tack on a risk premium and move into precautionary inventories, driving benchmark oil prices up within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
