<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_missile_strike_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising demand for compute expands access to high-performance accelerators and cloud training runs, accelerating development and deployment of autonomous guidance, target-recognition and swarm-control software that increases the tempo and effectiveness of drone and guided-missile operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="shipping_chokepoints::chokepoint_congestion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid spikes in AI compute demand create concentrated, time-sensitive shipments of GPUs, racks and servers through a small set of major ports and air hubs, producing immediate backlogs and berth/airspace shortages at those chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="shipping_chokepoints::global_freight_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated compute demand raises urgent cross-border movement of high-value accelerators and server equipment, expanding demand for premium container and airfreight capacity and pushing up short-term global freight price levels.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">shipping_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="us_china_tech_trade::component_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid increase in AI compute demand drives immediate, large-volume orders for GPUs/accelerators and server subsystems that draw down inventories and extend supplier lead times, reducing on‑hand and pipeline availability.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="us_china_tech_trade::supply_reconfig_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher compute requirements prompt cloud providers and OEMs to change sourcing and production footprints (nearshoring, dual-sourcing, contract reallocation) to secure chip and module supply, accelerating supply‑chain reconfiguration.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="us_iran_standoff::blockade_effectiveness" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising demand for compute accelerates deployment of AI-powered route‑optimization, low-latency sensor fusion and anomaly detection services by commercial shipping operators, enabling tankers to better predict, reroute and mask transits around interdiction zones and thereby reduce the effectiveness of blockades.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" target="us_iran_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher compute demand drives faster development and commercial availability of autonomous maritime drones, AI targeting and ISR systems that state and proxy actors can acquire or adapt, increasing the frequency of hostile encounters, boardings and interdictions in the corridor.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
