<edge source="shipping_chokepoints::supply_chain_resilience" target="ai_economic_shift::compute_demand_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">When supply-chain resilience falls and buying hardware becomes unreliable, firms shift workloads from planned on-prem purchases to leased cloud/colocation capacity, raising short-term demand intensity for cloud compute and accelerators.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">shipping_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_economic_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="shipping_chokepoints::supply_chain_resilience" target="us_china_tech_trade::supply_reconfig_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">When firms assess their supply chains as more resilient (reducing vulnerability to disruptions), they postpone or cancel active restructuring of sourcing and production footprints, lowering the observable reconfiguration rate.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">shipping_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
