  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater port handling capacity and redundant hinterland links allow ships to be offloaded, rerouted, or dispersed around interdictions, reducing the operational effectiveness of a blockade.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">shipping_chokepoints</data>
